		(uuid "ea37d1be-da8c-4bd8-94db-59714d0d7d64")
	)
	(text "1. D1-D3: 1N4007 used as PIN substitute (1 kV, standard recovery - NOT UF/fast types; Vishay/onsemi). D3 is biased\n   off with RF-derived HT, D2 only shunts leakage; all carry ~120 mA when on. Expect slightly higher RX loss / Ct than a real PIN.\n   D1 carries full TX RF only without K2 (RF-sense fault hold, PTT edges): ~2-4 W in DO-41 at 100 W - keep leads short,\n   solder to wide copper and test a 10 s RF-sense hold at 100 W into a dummy load (temperature, SWR) before use.\n   A series PIN that must stay OFF at HF needs reverse bias >= peak RF (100 W/50 ohm = 100 Vpk, ~150 Vpk at 2:1 SWR),\n   so D3 gets RF-derived bias: C45/D20/D21 double the TX RF into C46 (HT ~ 2 x RF peak, D22 clamps ~220 V).\n   D1/D2 only see RX-level RF when off, so +12 V is enough there. Bias lags RF by ~1-2 ms on 160 m (<0.2 ms 20 m+).\n   Bias 110-125 mA (R1 91R): stored charge >= 2 uC >> RF charge per half-cycle at 1.8 MHz / 100 W.\n   HIGH VOLTAGE (up to ~220 V DC during TX) on HT, C45-C46, D20-D22, R37, R3, Q3, C9 - keep creepage.\n2. K2 (G2RL-2, both poles in parallel, 2 x 8 A) bypasses C1-D1-C2 during PTT. PTT also forces the PIN switch to TX within us,\n   so K2 always closes/opens with the PIN path conducting (no hot-switching of K2 contacts).\n   Set radio TX delay >= 10 ms so K2 is closed before full power.\n3. IRF3708 (30 V, logic-level, TO-220) for the higher-current switches: Q1 (~120 mA PIN bias), Q8 (relay coils ~75 mA).\n   2N7000 (60 V, 200 mA) for low-current logic: Q10 (TXL -> TX), Q11 (Q3 gate shunt), Q12 (PTT inverter).\n   Q3 IRFP460 (500 V, TO-247): RXN low-side sink (D3 on in RX). No HV supply, no high-side switch needed.\n4. All parts through-hole. L1-L4: ~47 uH, ~10 T #24 on FT50-43 (T50 footprint). C1, C2: 220 nF 1 kV MKP film.\n   C3: 10 nF 1 kV C0G disc. C9, C20, C45, C46: 1 kV disc. D20/D21: UF4007 (1 kV fast). D22: P6KE220A. R1: 3 W. R3, R37: DIN0309 (>= 250 V).\n   J1-J3: coax soldered directly (Coax_SolderPads_RG58_RG316: braid pad + cable-tie holes; keep center lead <= 5 mm).\n   J4: 2.1 x 5.5 mm DC barrel jack (CUI PJ-102AH, center +). J6, J11-J14 (PTT IN 1-5, all in parallel), J10 (PTT OUT),\n   J8/J9 (AUDIO IN/OUT): RCA jacks Same Sky RCJ-01x (right angle PCB) - footprint from datasheet, check against a sample.\n5. Expected RF-sensed RX->TX time: D1/D2 on in ~5 us; D3 reverse bias follows the RF (doubler, ~0.2-2 ms by band).\n   No hang timer: under PTT the switch follows PTT (plus the instant RF path for the radio RF tail).\n   RF without PTT = fault: TX is held ~10 s after the last RF and D16 RF SENSED lights (inhibited during PTT + ~20 ms).\n6. Relay contact pinouts follow the KiCad symbols (K1 G5V-2: 4/13 COM, 6/11 NC, 8/9 NO; K2/K3 G2RL-2: 11/21 COM, 14/24 NO,\n   12/22 NC) - verify against the relay datasheet before layout.\n7. (HV module removed - D3 bias is RF-derived. Test 160 m at 100 W: D3 temperature and RX-port leakage at key-up.)\n8. K3 (G2RL-2 DPDT, coil across +12 V; pole 1 at RADIO, pole 2 at TX ANT): with no 12 V both NC contacts join RADIO to TX ANT via BYP,\n   and the whole switch is disconnected at both ends (no RF on unbiased PIN diodes).\n   With 12 V applied both K3 NO contacts insert the switch; RX ANT is only ever reached through the powered PIN path.\n9. SW1 RX ANT ON/OFF (panel toggle in the K3 coil feed): OFF = K3 released = RADIO -> TX ANT direct in any condition.\n   SW1, D6 (TX) and D16 (RF SENSED) are panel mounted at the RADIO end, on 2.54 mm pin headers (LED pin 1 = K, pin 2 = A).\n   Losing 12 V during TX hot-switches K3 (RF moves to the BYP path); K3 pulls in ~10 ms after power-up. G2RL-2 contacts: 8 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 219.71 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "80c3c8d9-180d-4096-aef2-89d3355aea2f")
	)
